From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: sun8i: A733 init per the UM, query mode, no data interrupt

The A733 entry reused sun50i_h6_thermal_init(). Two of its writes are the
H6's, not this part's, and one of them costs idle power.

WHAT THE UM SAYS

A733 UM V1.00 7.1.6.1 (p. 344, PDF p. 365), query mode, steps 3-9:
THS_CTRL acquire time 0x2F in [15:0] and sample divider 0x1DF in [31:16];
THS_PER 0x3A in [31:12]; THS_FILTER enable (bit 2) and type 1 (average of
4); calibration into THSn_CDATA; THS_EN last. Interrupt mode adds
THS_DATA_INTC. The THS chapter of UM V0.92 is word for word the same (575
extracted text lines, no difference).

THS_PER is 4096 * (n + 1) / CLK_IN per conversion (7.1.8.3, p. 346). With
the filter averaging four conversions and five sensors sharing the block,
one sensor gets a new word every 4096 * (n + 1) * 4 * 5 / 24 MHz:
0.201 s for 0x3A, 1.249 s for the H6's 365.

One defect in the chapter: the THS_CTRL table (7.1.8.1, p. 345) puts
TACQ, the ADC acquire time with its 2 us default, in bits 31:16 and marks bits 15:0 reserved.
Only the programming guide's reading gives 2 us (48 cycles at 24 MHz); the
table's would be 480 cycles, 20 us. The reset value, the vendor driver and
this driver all follow the guide.

WHAT THE SILICON SAYS (Cubie A7S, 6 GiB board, 2026-09-25)

- Reset defaults, read after asserting and releasing THS0_BGR live, before
  any driver write: THS_CTRL 0x01DF002F, THS_EN 0, THS_PER 0x0003A000,
  THS_DATA_INTC 0, THS_FILTER 0x1, THS0_ALARM_CTRL 0x05A00684,
  THS0_THS1_CDATA 0x08000800 -- all as the UM tables state. The UM's
  period is the hardware's own reset value.
- The period formula at two points: predicted 4.00 and 24.83 data IRQs/s
  for n = 365 and 0x3A, measured 4.0 and 24.8.
- Writing THS_PER while THS_EN is set stops conversion (no IRQ, frozen
  values) until THS_EN is cleared and set again. This init writes THS_EN
  last, as the UM orders it.
- Idle at the greeter, 30 s per arm, values set live:

    THS_PER  data IRQ  IRQ/s  A55 freq transitions  zone0 changes in 5 s
    365      on        4.0    226                   4
    0x3A     on        24.8   1089                  28
    0x3A     off       0.0    116                   25

WHY NO DATA INTERRUPT

The zones are polled by the thermal core (polling-delay 1000 ms,
polling-delay-passive 500 ms), and a poll reads the live THSn_DATA word, so
the interrupt only adds wakeups. Each wakes the SCHED_FIFO irq thread, and
without CONFIG_UCLAMP_TASK schedutil raises the A55 policy to the top OPP
for it -- the idle frequency churn found in an earlier investigation. At the UM period that is
24.8 wakeups/s and five times today's churn; without the interrupt, half of
today's. A first read before the first conversion returns -EAGAIN, which the
core rechecks after THERMAL_RECHECK_DELAY (thermal_zone_recheck()).
THS_DATA_INTC is written 0 rather than left at its reset value, so nothing a
previous owner enabled survives. The IRQ stays requested; it never fires.

The comments on the A733 chip entry and on the trend filter described the
old period and are rewritten; the trend filter's noise figures were
measured at 1.25 s and are labelled so.

Verified: applies at fuzz 0, builds (W=1 clean). Pending on silicon: the
register readback after boot (THS_PER 0x0003A000, THS_FILTER 0x5,
THS_DATA_INTC 0), no THS interrupts, zones updating about five times a
second, and the trip behaviour at 90 C under load against the H6 init
(the falsifier of a separate, earlier investigation) -- including whether the trend filter's trend_hyst
still fits the noise at the shorter period.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff -uNr a/drivers/thermal/sun8i_thermal.c b/drivers/thermal/sun8i_thermal.c
--- a/drivers/thermal/sun8i_thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/sun8i_thermal.c
@@ -206,20 +206,16 @@
  * samples.  On this part that is a one-bit differentiator fed a signal it
  * cannot resolve, for two measured reasons.
  *
- * The sensors are slow as this driver programs them -- a choice, not a
- * property of the part.  sun50i_h6_thermal_init() writes THS_PER = 365 (the
- * H6 value; the UM's init sequence writes 0x3A = 58, the vendor driver 28)
- * at 24 MHz, so one conversion takes 4096 * 366 / 24e6 = 62.5 ms; THS_FILTER
- * averages four of them and the five sensors share the block, which puts a
- * new word in each THSn_DATA every 4096 * 366 * 4 * 5 / 24e6 = 1.2493 s.
- * Measured on a Cubie A7S: every reported value holds for 1.22..1.26 s, and
- * the shared data interrupt fires at 4.00 /s, i.e. 0.8 Hz per sensor.  A CPU
- * zone polls at 500 ms, so at this period two out of three governor cycles see
- * no new sensor data at all -- shortening the poll cannot help, and
- * lengthening it costs response.
+ * The sensor cadence is set by sun60i_a733_thermal_init(): THS_PER = 0x3A,
+ * the UM's value and the register's reset default, so one conversion takes
+ * 4096 * 59 / 24e6 = 10.07 ms; THS_FILTER averages four of them and the five
+ * sensors share the block, which puts a new word in each THSn_DATA every
+ * 4096 * 59 * 4 * 5 / 24e6 = 0.201 s.  Every 500 ms governor cycle therefore
+ * reads a fresh value.  (Until 2026-09-25 the reused H6 init wrote 365, a
+ * 1.25 s update, and two of three cycles saw no new data at all.)
  *
  * The sensors are noisy.  Detrended inside sliding 10 s windows, pooled over
- * six full-load runs, the residual on the two CPU zones is 0.93 K and
+ * six full-load runs at the old 1.25 s period, the residual on the two CPU zones is 0.93 K and
  * 1.23 K RMS, with a 90th-percentile peak-to-peak of 4.9 K and 6.3 K.  The
  * same magnitude appears on the DDR, NPU and GPU sensors under a CPU-only load,
  * and the residuals are uncorrelated between sensors, so this is not the die
@@ -666,6 +662,45 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * A733: the UM's init sequence in query mode (A733 UM V1.00 7.1.6.1, steps
+ * 3-9, p. 344; identical in V0.92).  Every value written here is also the
+ * register's reset default except THS_FILTER's enable bit, read back on a
+ * Cubie A7S after a live THS0_BGR reset.
+ *
+ *  - THS_CTRL: acquire time 0x2F in [15:0], sample divider 0x1DF in [31:16]
+ *    (steps 3-4).  The UM's register table labels the two halves the other
+ *    way round; only the programming guide's reading gives its own 2 us.
+ *  - THS_PER = 0x3A (step 5): 4096 * 59 / 24 MHz = 10.07 ms per conversion,
+ *    0.201 s per sensor update with the filter and five sensors.  The H6
+ *    init's 365 gave 1.25 s.
+ *  - THS_FILTER: enabled, average of 4 (steps 6-7).
+ *  - Calibration (step 8) has run in sun8i_ths_resource_init() already.
+ *  - No data interrupt.  The zones are polled by the thermal core, and a poll
+ *    reads the live THSn_DATA word, so a per-sample interrupt adds nothing but
+ *    wakeups: 24.8 /s at this period, each waking the SCHED_FIFO irq thread,
+ *    for which schedutil raises the A55 policy.  Measured idle on a Cubie A7S:
+ *    1089 A55 frequency transitions in 30 s with the interrupt, 116 without
+ *    (226 with the H6 init).  THS_DATA_INTC is cleared explicitly so that
+ *    nothing a previous owner left enabled survives.
+ */
+static int sun60i_a733_thermal_init(struct ths_device *tmdev)
+{
+	regmap_write(tmdev->regmap, SUN50I_THS_CTRL0,
+		     SUN50I_THS_CTRL0_T_ACQ(48) |
+		     SUN50I_THS_CTRL0_T_SAMPLE_PER(480));
+	regmap_write(tmdev->regmap, SUN50I_H6_THS_PC,
+		     SUN50I_H6_THS_PC_TEMP_PERIOD(0x3a));
+	regmap_write(tmdev->regmap, SUN50I_H6_THS_MFC,
+		     SUN50I_THS_FILTER_EN |
+		     SUN50I_THS_FILTER_TYPE(1));
+	regmap_write(tmdev->regmap, SUN50I_H6_THS_DIC, 0);
+	regmap_write(tmdev->regmap, SUN50I_H6_THS_ENABLE,
+		     GENMASK(tmdev->chip->sensor_num - 1, 0));
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int sun8i_ths_register(struct ths_device *tmdev)
 {
 	int i;
@@ -871,10 +906,9 @@
  * the DT cell becomes sensor[i].id and addresses temp_data_base + 4 * i.
  * Register-compatible with the H6 layout: every SUN50I_H6_*
  * offset lands on a live, correctly shaped register on this part, and the
- * vendor driver programs CTRL0 and MFC with the same constants this driver
- * writes. THS_PER (SUN50I_H6_THS_PC) is not the same: the reused
- * sun50i_h6_thermal_init() writes 365, the vendor 28, the UM's init sequence
- * 0x3A = 58 -- 1.25 s per sensor update here against 0.10 s and 0.20 s.
+ * vendor driver programs CTRL0 and MFC with the same constants. The init is
+ * its own, sun60i_a733_thermal_init(), because THS_PER and the data
+ * interrupt are not the H6's -- see there.
  *
  * Two clocks: the bus gate, and a 24 MHz conversion clock that the ADC needs
  * and whose CCU reset default is OFF -- hence has_mod_clk as well as
@@ -906,7 +940,7 @@
 	.trend_hyst = 6000,
 	.temp_data_base = SUN50I_H6_THS_TEMP_DATA,
 	.calibrate = sun50i_h6_ths_calibrate,
-	.init = sun50i_h6_thermal_init,
+	.init = sun60i_a733_thermal_init,
 	.irq_ack = sun50i_h6_irq_ack,
 	.calc_temp = sun60i_a733_calc_temp,
 };
